<title>USA: US Home Builders-Market Index falls to 54 in May.</title>
<headline>US Home Builders-Market Index falls to 54 in May.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Association of Home Builders said its Housing Market Index fell two points to 54 in May from 56 in April.</p>
<p>Builders' ratings of single-family home sales fell to 57 from 59 in April.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, traffic of prospective buyers declined one point to 44 in May from 45 in April. And the component index for single-family sales in the next six months dipped to 62 from 63 during the same period.  </p>
<p>A Housing Market Index over 50 generally means the number of positive responses received from builders exceeded the number of negative responses. The May index is based on the ratings of 270 respondents.</p>
